[2026-04-05 15:18:05] Finalized the manual-grounded BOOTCFG and USER_REG0-3 summary and API recommendation.
Documentation basis:
- Extracted text from Documents/tm4c129xnczad.pdf at progress/manual_extract_2026-04-05_15-12-30/tm4c129xnczad.txt.
- Chapter 8 Internal Memory, section 8.2.3.12 Non-Volatile Register Programming-- Flash Memory Resident Registers (page 646).
- Section 8.6 Memory Register Descriptions (System Control Offset) (page 700).
- BOOTCFG register map/description pages 706-709, with TOC/register map anchor page 707.
- USER_REG0-3 register description page 710.
Conclusions:
- BOOTCFG is documented as RO from the SYSCTL address space and is not written directly; programming belongs to the Flash programming path through FMD/FMC and requires POR to take effect.
- USER_REG0-3 are documented in the register map as W0, while the DATA field is shown as RW. The family is readable and writable for staged values with 1-to-0 programming semantics and one-time non-volatile commitment behavior.
- The current repo already keeps non-volatile register commit mechanics in FLASH and exposes narrow getter-style SYSCTL APIs. Recommended public surface: BOOTCFG read-side semantic getters only, if exposed at all; USER_REG staged getters only by default, with any staging setter or commit path kept explicitly separated and the commit operation owned by FLASH.
Status: ready to report to user.
